        <string key="rules.tiles.title" text="Tiles"/>
        <string key="rules.tiles.line1" text="The set has {tiles} tiles: three suits ({dots}, {bamboo}, {characters}) running from one to {ranks}, four winds and three dragons, {copies} copies of each."/>
        <string key="rules.tiles.line2" text="Ones and nines are terminals, twos to eights are simples, winds and dragons are honours. Terminals and honours are worth more in scoring."/>
        <string key="rules.tiles.line3" text="Winds and dragons only go into pungs, kongs and pairs: they never form a chow."/>
        <string key="rules.tiles.line4" text="This game is played without flowers and seasons."/>
        <string key="rules.sets.title" text="Sets and a winning hand"/>
        <string key="rules.sets.line1" text="A winning hand is {winning} tiles: four sets and a pair. You hold {dealt} tiles and win with the one tile that completes them."/>
        <string key="rules.sets.line2" text="A chow is three tiles of one suit in a row; it never uses honours and never wraps round from a nine to a one."/>
        <string key="rules.sets.line3" text="A pung is three equal tiles. A kong is four equal tiles and counts as one set. A pair is two equal tiles."/>
        <string key="rules.sets.line4" text="Two special hands need no sets: {pairs} different pairs, and the {orphans} orphans (one of each terminal and honour, and one of them twice)."/>
        <string key="rules.sets.line5" text="Special hands win only when no set has been laid out. Below: a chow, a pung, a chow, a pung of dragons and a pair."/>
        <string key="rules.turn.title" text="A turn"/>
        <string key="rules.turn.line1" text="Each seat holds {dealt} tiles. On your turn you draw a tile from the wall (the game does it for you) and discard one, back to {dealt}."/>
        <string key="rules.turn.line2" text="Click a tile of your hand to discard it; the tile you have just drawn lies apart at the right end. East, the dealer, starts with {winning} tiles."/>
        <string key="rules.turn.line3" text="Discards lie in front of their seat in the order thrown, and everyone sees them. The turn goes counter-clockwise to the next seat."/>
        <string key="rules.turn.line4" text="The buttons ({pung}, {kong}, {chow}, {pass}, {mahjong}, {declare}) appear only when that move is possible; point at one to read what it does."/>
        <string key="rules.claims.title" text="Claims and their priority"/>
        <string key="rules.claims.line1" text="When a seat discards, the others may take the tile out of turn if it completes a set; if nobody can, the next seat draws at once."/>
        <string key="rules.claims.line2" text="{chow}: a run of three, only for the seat right after the discarder. {pung}: three equal tiles, from any seat. {kong}: four equal tiles, from any seat."/>
        <string key="rules.claims.line3" text="{mahjong}: the tile completes your hand; you must have declared the ready hand first (see the page about the calling hand)."/>
        <string key="rules.claims.line4" text="Priority: {mahjong} first, then {pung} or {kong}, then {chow}. Two claims of {mahjong}: the seat farther counter-clockwise from the discarder wins."/>
        <string key="rules.claims.line5" text="A claimed set is laid face up and its owner discards without drawing; after a kong a loose tile is drawn. {pass} lets the tile go; each seat decides once."/>
        <string key="rules.kongs.title" text="Kongs and the loose tile"/>
        <string key="rules.kongs.line1" text="A kong is four equal tiles, made three ways: {kong} on a discard when you hold three, {kong} from four equal tiles of your hand, or {upgrade} to an open pung."/>
        <string key="rules.kongs.line2" text="A pung is upgraded only with the tile you have just drawn from the wall, not with one that you kept from an earlier turn."/>
        <string key="rules.kongs.line3" text="After a kong you draw a loose tile from the reserve of {loose} tiles at the break of the wall; the reserve is refilled from the end of the live wall."/>
        <string key="rules.kongs.line4" text="The last {deadWall} tiles of the wall are the dead wall and are never drawn."/>
        <string key="rules.kongs.line5" text="A kong added to a pung can be robbed: a seat with a declared ready hand that the tile completes may take it with {mahjong} and wins."/>
        <string key="rules.calling.title" text="The calling hand"/>
        <string key="rules.calling.line1" text="A hand is calling when one tile more completes it: {dealt} tiles that wait for a winning tile. Below: this hand waits for two kinds."/>
        <string key="rules.calling.line2" text="To declare it press {declare}, then click the tile to discard; the {dealt} tiles that stay must be waiting."/>
        <string key="rules.calling.line3" text="Without the declaration you cannot win, on a discard or on your own draw. After it you are not bound to keep the hand."/>
        <string key="rules.calling.line4" text="Declaring with your first discard of the hand scores extra."/>
        <string key="rules.calling.line5" text="With the hints on, the row inside the wall shows the tiles your hand waits for and how many copies you cannot see."/>
        <string key="rules.end.title" text="The end of a hand"/>
        <string key="rules.end.line1" text="A hand ends when somebody wins, or when the live wall is empty at a draw: a drawn hand, nobody pays."/>
        <string key="rules.end.line2" text="You win with {mahjong} on a discard, on your own draw (self-draw) or by robbing a kong; the hand must be a winning hand and the ready hand declared."/>
        <string key="rules.end.line3" text="A drawn hand is played again with the same dealer and does not count as a hand of the match."/>
        <string key="rules.end.line4" text="After a win the score table shows what each seat scored, the winner's lines and the change of points; press {nextHand} to go on."/>
